from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'dist'
updated='19 October 2026'
contact='<a href="mailto:sales@storywell.in">sales@storywell.in</a>'
pages={
 'terms':('Terms of use',f'''<p>Chromalie is a free browser colouring studio operated by StoryWell Books. These terms describe the permitted use of the studio and its library. Contact {contact} with questions.</p>
<h2>Using the studio</h2><p>You can choose a page, colour it, save progress in your browser and download your work. There is no visitor account, subscription or checkout. Chromalie does not ask for payment details.</p><p>Use the site lawfully. Do not attempt to interfere with its operation, bypass access controls or introduce harmful code. Adults should guide young people when they use the internet and handle any contact with us on their behalf.</p>
<h2>Artwork and permitted reuse</h2><p>You may use the colouring tools and keep your finished work for personal, home and classroom use, subject to the rights and licence terms that apply to the underlying illustration. Downloading a picture does not transfer copyright in that illustration.</p><p>Rights in original artwork remain with its respective rights holders. The Chromalie name, site design and original site content are separate from the supplied illustrations. The Chromalie footer identifies the studio through which a page was coloured; it does not claim authorship of the underlying drawing.</p><p>A licence permitting the sale, redistribution or commercial reuse of an illustration must be obtained from the relevant rights holder. These terms do not grant a blanket licence to sell or repackage the uncoloured library. If you believe an illustration should be removed or credited differently, use the <a href="contact.html">rights contact</a>.</p>
<h2>Your saved work</h2><p>Artwork and custom colours save on your device when device saving is enabled. Clearing site data, changing browser, using a private window or visiting a different website address can affect access to those saves. A download remains on your device independently of browser storage.</p><p>You can download a PNG for viewing and printing or an editable project file for reopening in Chromalie. You are responsible for keeping copies you wish to retain. Undo history is available while a page is open and is not a permanent archive.</p>
<h2>Availability and limitations</h2><p>We may update the tools and library. Brush textures approximate drawing media. Shape detection can be affected by faint, open or broken outlines. Device and browser differences can affect the experience. We do not promise uninterrupted availability or error-free operation.</p><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, StoryWell Books is not responsible for loss arising from unavailable service or lost device saves. Nothing in these terms excludes liability or rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
<h2>Sharing</h2><p>The Share button hands your coloured page to your device’s own share menu, or opens WhatsApp. Chromalie does not receive the picture; what happens to it after that is governed by the app you choose.</p><h2>Privacy and links</h2><p>Read our <a href="privacy.html">privacy notice</a> and <a href="cookies.html">cookies and storage notice</a>. Linked third-party sites and hosting services have their own terms and privacy practices.</p>
<h2>Law, changes and contact</h2><p>Indian law applies to these terms, subject to mandatory protections and jurisdiction rules that apply to you. The courts with jurisdiction under applicable law may hear disputes. Please contact {contact} first so that we can try to resolve a problem.</p><p>We will date changes to these terms on this page. Changes apply prospectively, subject to applicable law.</p>'''),
 'privacy':('Privacy notice',f'''<p>StoryWell Books operates Chromalie. This notice explains the information used by the studio and the choices available to you. Our privacy contact is {contact}.</p>
<h2>Colouring stays in your browser</h2><p>Chromalie’s application code does not upload your paint layers, custom palette or editable project files to StoryWell Books. There is no visitor account, public gallery, messaging feature or contact form. When you share a page, it goes from your device to the app you choose; it does not pass through StoryWell Books.</p><p>When device saving is enabled, the browser stores your coloured paint layers, page identifiers, saved thumbnails and save times. Your custom palette also saves locally. The browser keeps these until you clear them or it removes site data. See <a href="index.html#storage">storage settings</a> to switch off new saves or clear saved artwork and palettes.</p><p>A setting remembers your choice about device saving. Another setting remembers whether you have dismissed the storage notice. These settings are kept on your browser so that your choices can be respected. Undo history and temporary drawing information are held during a session.</p><p>PNG downloads and editable project files are created on your device. Opening an editable project reads that file in your browser; the application does not send it to a server.</p>
<h2>Hosting information</h2><p>A host must receive requests to deliver the site. Hosting providers may process technical request information, including an IP address, browser information, requested files and request times, for delivery, reliability and security.</p><p>Chromalie at chromalie.page is served by Netlify, which receives and may log visitors’ IP addresses and request details to deliver the site and keep it secure. See <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" rel="noreferrer">Netlify’s privacy policy</a>. The earlier address varnasr.github.io/Chromalie was served by GitHub Pages and now forwards to chromalie.page; GitHub’s own practices are in <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noreferrer">its privacy statement</a>. A still earlier version on chatgpt.site was hosted through OpenAI’s Sites service; see <a href="https://openai.com/policies/row-privacy-policy/" rel="noreferrer">OpenAI’s privacy policy</a>.</p><p>Provider retention and processing arrangements apply to this technical information. We do not promise that all hosting or support data is stored in India. This studio has no advertising scripts and no analytics beyond the anonymous counts described below.</p>
<h2>Anonymous counts</h2><p>To know whether Chromalie is used, the site adds one to a daily tally when the site is opened, when a page is opened (recorded by collection, such as Owls), and when a page is downloaded, printed or shared, the journal is opened or saved as a PDF, or Chromalie is installed. Each tally is a date, the kind of event and, where there is one, the collection. Nothing else is sent: no cookie, no identifier, no page title, no picture and nothing you type. The tallies are stored with Supabase, in its Mumbai region, and StoryWell Books can read only the totals for each day.</p><p>Supabase, like any service that receives a request, sees the request’s IP address and browser information when a tally is sent, and keeps them in its own short-lived request logs under <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" rel="noreferrer">its privacy policy</a>. They are not stored with the tally. If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, Chromalie sends no tallies at all.</p><h2>If you contact us</h2><p>If you email StoryWell Books, we receive your email address, the contents of your message and anything you attach. We use this information to respond to your request, investigate a reported problem or rights claim, and meet applicable legal obligations. Our email service provider processes the correspondence needed to deliver and store it.</p><p>We keep correspondence while handling a request and for any follow-up, dispute or legal obligation that requires it. We review whether it remains necessary. Please avoid sending information that is unrelated to your request.</p>
<h2>Young people</h2><p>The studio does not ask for a date of birth, identity documents or a child’s contact information. It has no public chat or profile feature. Parents or guardians should handle support requests for young children and avoid including identifying information about them.</p>
<h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>You can switch off new device saves, clear saved work, and download copies using the studio controls. Clearing browser site data is another way to remove local records. StoryWell Books cannot remotely clear your browser’s saved drawings.</p><p>Depending on the laws that apply, you may have rights to access, correct or erase personal information held about you; restrict or object to its use; withdraw consent where use relies on consent; and complain to the relevant authority. Send requests about information held by StoryWell Books to {contact}. Requests concerning a provider’s own records should be sent to that provider.</p><p>We will assess requests and respond within the period required by applicable law. We may need proportionate information to verify a request. These choices do not remove records we must lawfully retain.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2><p>We will update this notice if the studio’s data practices change and date the revised notice here. A new account, cloud-save, further analytics or public-sharing feature would require a fresh review before introduction.</p>'''),
 'cookies':('Cookies & device storage',f'''<p>Chromalie’s application code does not set advertising or analytics cookies. It uses browser storage for colouring and your preferences. Hosting services may use their own essential security or delivery cookies.</p>
<h2>What the studio stores</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Storage</th><th>Purpose</th><th>How long</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Saved artwork and palette</td><td>Let you return to coloured pages and reuse custom colours when device saving is enabled</td><td>Until cleared by you or removed by the browser</td></tr><tr><td>Device-saving choice</td><td>Respect whether you want new artwork and palettes saved</td><td>Until changed or browser site data is cleared</td></tr><tr><td>Notice preference</td><td>Remember that you have dismissed the storage notice, the first-visit tour or the note about keeping saves on an iPhone or iPad</td><td>Until browser site data is cleared</td></tr><tr><td>Temporary drawing data</td><td>Support an open page, selections and undo</td><td>During the open session</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Choose what saves</h2><p><a class="button" href="index.html#storage">Open storage settings</a></p><p>Turning device saving off stops new artwork and custom palette saves. Earlier saved work remains available until you clear it. The saving choice itself is remembered so that the browser can respect it.</p><p>You can clear Chromalie’s saved artwork and custom palette through the settings. This also resets the open page. Download work you wish to keep before clearing it. The studio cannot remove cookies set by another host or service; manage these through that service or your browser settings.</p>
<h2>Hosting and third parties</h2><p>Technical requests to a hosting service are necessary to load this website. On chromalie.page, Netlify receives visitor IP addresses to deliver and secure the site. The earlier GitHub Pages address, which now forwards here, and the earlier chatgpt.site version had their own hosting arrangements. Read the <a href="privacy.html">privacy notice</a> and the relevant provider’s privacy information.</p><p>The studio has no advertising trackers or embedded social-media feeds. It sends anonymous daily counts, described in the <a href="privacy.html">privacy notice</a>, which use no cookie and no browser storage, and which stop when your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control. The storage notice is an explanation of device-saving behaviour. Dismissing it does not authorise advertising or any further analytics.</p>
<h2>Browser controls</h2><p>Your browser can block or clear site storage. Blocking it can prevent saved work and preferences from surviving a session; colouring and downloads remain available where the browser supports them. Storage permissions and private-browsing behaviour vary by browser.</p><p>Questions about these choices can be sent to {contact}.</p>'''),
 'accessibility':('Accessibility',f'''<p>We want Chromalie’s menus, instructions and controls to be readable and usable. We are improving the studio as people use it and report problems.</p>
<h2>What is available</h2><p>The site has larger text for navigation, page details and instructions, keyboard focus indicators, labels for controls, a skip link, responsive layouts and support for reduced-motion preferences. Text can be enlarged through the browser’s zoom controls.</p><p>The studio includes brush-size, opacity and smoothing controls, zoom and pan, undo and redo, automatic area clipping, and a focus view that gives the drawing more space. Controls use text and labels as well as colour swatches.</p>
<h2>Current limitations</h2><p>Direct colouring uses a mouse, touch input or stylus. The drawing canvas is not fully operable through a keyboard or screen reader. Illustrations have collection and subject labels; detailed descriptions of individual drawing elements are not yet available.</p><p>We have not completed an independent accessibility audit and do not claim a certified conformance level. Browser and assistive-technology differences may affect the experience.</p>
<h2>Report a problem</h2><p>Email {contact} with the page or control involved, your browser and any assistive technology you use. Include only the information needed to explain the problem. We will review the report and discuss available alternatives where possible.</p>'''),
 'contact':('Contact & artwork rights',f'''<p>Chromalie is operated by StoryWell Books.</p><p><a class="contact-email" href="mailto:sales@storywell.in">sales@storywell.in</a></p>
<h2>Help with the studio</h2><p>For a problem with colouring, saving or downloads, include the collection and page number, your browser, and what happened. A screenshot may help. Do not send passwords or payment information.</p>
<h2>Privacy requests</h2><p>Send privacy questions and requests concerning information held by StoryWell Books to the email above. You can manage local artwork through <a href="index.html#storage">storage settings</a>. Our <a href="privacy.html">privacy notice</a> explains the distinction between browser saves, correspondence and hosting records.</p>
<h2>Artwork rights and attribution</h2><p>If you believe an illustration has been included without the required permission or needs a credit corrected, identify the affected collection and page, explain your rights or authority to act, and provide supporting information. We will review the claim and take appropriate action.</p><p>The Chromalie footer marks the colouring studio. It does not replace an artist credit or establish ownership of an illustration.</p>''')
}
links='<a href="terms.html">Terms of use</a><a href="privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="cookies.html">Cookies &amp; storage</a><a href="index.html#storage">Storage settings</a><a href="accessibility.html">Accessibility</a><a href="contact.html">Contact &amp; rights</a>'
for slug,(title,body) in pages.items():
 html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#faf8f3"><meta name="description" content="{escape(title)} for Chromalie, a colouring studio operated by StoryWell Books."><title>{escape(title)} | Chromalie</title><link rel="icon" href="icon.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="legal.css"></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#policy-content">Skip to the notice</a><header class="legal-header"><a href="index.html" aria-label="Chromalie home"><img src="wordmark.svg" alt="Chromalie"></a><a href="index.html">Back to colouring</a></header><main class="policy-page" id="policy-content"><p class="policy-date">StoryWell Books · Updated {updated}</p><h1>{escape(title)}</h1>{body}</main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><div><a class="footer-brand" href="index.html">chromalie.</a><p>A colouring studio by StoryWell Books.</p></div><div class="footer-contact">{contact}</div></div><nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Legal and privacy">{links}</nav><div class="footer-bottom"><span>© 2026 StoryWell Books. Artwork rights remain with their respective holders.</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div></footer></body></html>'''
 (root/(slug+'.html')).write_text(html)
print('Five legal and contact pages created.')
